  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRG: PIDR Global Labor Program - New Frontiers in Advancing Labor Rights (GLP-NFALR)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Bureau for Development, Democracy, and Innovation (D):  The Global Labor Program - New Frontiers in Advancing Labor Rights (GLP-NFALR) advances labor rights and builds the capacity of worker organizations, which are key civil society actors. GLP-NFALR supports governance, rule of law, economic growth, human rights, counter trafficking in persons, disability inclusion, and gender equality objectives by increasing decent work worldwide. GLP-NFALR is managed out of the DRG Center in close coordination with activity managers at USAID Missions. GLP-NFALR will deepen USAID&apos;s engagement with local labor actors to address both traditional and emerging issues in the labor sector globally, such as migration, informal work, forced labor, climate change, inclusion, and closing civic space. The activity supports U.S. national security and trade priorities and advances a foreign policy for the American middle class by addressing abusive labor practices overseas that undermine the competitiveness of U.S. workers, and by supporting U.S. trade priorities to monitor and enforce worker rights provisions of trade agreements and global supply chain standards. GLP-NFALR is implemented by the Solidarity Center. GLP-NFALR directly contributes to the Multilateral Partnership for Organizing, Worker Empowerment, and Rights (M-POWER) initiative, which is a key deliverable of the Presidential Initiative for Democratic Renewal (PIDR) that USAID collaborates on with the Department of Labor and U.S. Department of State&apos;s Bureau for Democracy, Rights, and Labor (DRL). FY 2022 resources will be used to support GLP-NFALR programming in approximately 30 countries spanning five regions, using worker-centric implementation modalities including research, organizing, collective bargaining, communications support, legal defense and support, trade union strengthening and strategic planning, inclusive leadership development, strategic networking, stakeholder engagement and advocacy, and resiliency cap</narrative>
  </description>
